---
scope: src/cli/hook
alignment: unreviewed
description: "Terminal entry called by Claude Code hooks that turns each hook call into session presence and pings a running observer, fast, silent and never failing the agent."
intent: >
  Claude Code runs hooks itself, apart from the aide server, when a session
  starts, on each prompt and tool call, when the agent stops and when the
  session ends. This entry turns each call into that session's presence
  (working, waiting on the user, or ended) with the time, records it, then
  pings a running observer so open pages update live. It exists only to
  report presence: it returns fast, prints nothing meant for a person, and
  never fails, blocks or slows the agent's work, whatever goes wrong.
outcomes:
  desired:
    - A session start, a prompt or a tool call records the session as working, the agent stopping records it as waiting on the user, and the session's end records it ended, each with the hook's time.
    - Presence is recorded before any attempt to reach the observer, so it survives the observer being off, and a running observer is pinged so open pages show the change without a reload.
    - Every call exits successfully and fast, whether recording, pinging or reading the hook's input fails, so the agent's work never waits on it or breaks because of it.
    - Presence lands in per-user storage outside the project, under the hook's own session and project, apart from that session's report log.
  undesired:
    - A hook call that fails, errors, prompts or takes long enough to slow the agent, including when the observer is down or the hook's input is malformed.
    - Presence written into the project, or into a session's report log so that log gains a second writer.
    - A hook call that starts the observer, ends any session but its own, or deletes any record.
    - Presence recorded under the wrong session or project, or the agent stopping recorded as ended, so a session waiting on the user reads as closed.
---
